[Start "1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4"]

3... h6 4. c3 { Prepares d4. Black spent a move on h6, so there is no hurry and White can build a strong centre. } 4... Nf6 ( 4... Bc5 5. d4 { Hits the bishop and takes the centre now that Black has not castled. } 5... exd4 6. cxd4 ) 5. d3 { Guards e4 and keeps the position calm. } 5... d6 6. O-O { Gets the king safe. } 6... Be7 7. Re1 { Defends e4 so the knight on f3 is free to move. Plan: Nbd2, Nf1 and Ng3, then d4 when the pieces are ready. } *
